From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2-gl: no texture upload for a surface that is not on
 the screen

In scanout mode the window shows the guest's texture and the console
surface is not drawn, but every new surface was still uploaded with
glTexImage2D. virgl_cmd_set_scanout makes a new surface whenever the
guest changes its primary's rectangle. On the Raspberry Pi 4, a 720p60
video in a WebView full screen does that about ten times in ten minutes,
and each SET_SCANOUT then held the BQL for 15-31 ms of main-loop CPU
(13.6 ms of a 14.5 ms resize was the upload). Make the texture when the
surface is drawn instead: leaving scanout mode already does, and
sdl2_gl_render_surface now does if it is missing.

Measured with a build of the same change that also logged its timings.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 ui/sdl2-gl.c | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/sdl2-gl.c b/ui/sdl2-gl.c
index cec7558eb..a70dd1c43 100644
--- a/ui/sdl2-gl.c
+++ b/ui/sdl2-gl.c
@@ -55,6 +55,8 @@ static void sdl2_gl_render_surface(struct sdl2_console *scon)
     int ww, wh;
 
     SDL_GL_MakeCurrent(scon->real_window, scon->winctx);
+    /* q11-102: sdl2_gl_switch leaves it to the first draw in scanout mode */
+    surface_gl_create_texture(scon->gls, scon->surface);
 
     SDL_GetWindowSize(scon->real_window, &ww, &wh);
     surface_gl_setup_viewport(scon->gls, scon->surface, ww, wh);
@@ -108,7 +110,20 @@ void sdl2_gl_switch(DisplayChangeListener *dcl,
         sdl2_window_resize(scon);
     }
 
-    surface_gl_create_texture(scon->gls, scon->surface);
+    /*
+     * q11-102: no upload for a surface that is not on the screen. In scanout
+     * mode the window shows the guest's texture (guest_fb), and the surface is
+     * drawn again only after sdl2_set_scanout_mode(false), which makes its
+     * texture, or by sdl2_gl_render_surface, which makes it if it is missing.
+     * virgl_cmd_set_scanout resizes the console (a new surface) whenever the
+     * guest changes its primary's rectangle. On the RPi4, WebView 720p60 full
+     * screen switches it between 1280x720 and 1280x599+0+60 about ten times in
+     * ten minutes, and each SET_SCANOUT then held the BQL for 15-31 ms of
+     * main-loop CPU; the texture upload was 13.6 ms of a 14.5 ms resize.
+     */
+    if (!scon->scanout_mode) {
+        surface_gl_create_texture(scon->gls, scon->surface);
+    }
 }
 
 void sdl2_gl_refresh(DisplayChangeListener *dcl)
